   "does": "On pull requests only, and even when an earlier step failed (unless the run was cancelled): runs make codemap-setup (a no-op when the venv already works) and then `codemap.py impact --base origin/$GITHUB_BASE_REF` with the venv interpreter, which writes the impact list for the PR's changes (callers up to triggers, tests, docs, shared state; no findings, since the overlay is local only) to the job summary. Not a gate: it exits 0 whenever the base ref resolves. Setting up its own interpreter keeps it working when an earlier step failed and the code map check never created the venv.",
   "entry": "gates.yml workflow on pull_request, script-gates job",
